# arvo-storage. Backlog

Designed-but-deferred items for the L0 storage crate. Names stay
unbacktickd until they ship.

## ConstParamTy on UFixed / IFixed

Manual ConstParamTy_ impl on UFixed and IFixed lets fixed-point types
appear directly as const generic arguments. Verified-friction in
rustc 1.96-nightly per the round 202604271346 Q-A spike scope notes.
Lands when the friction clears or the workaround pattern stabilises.

## USize as Bits-rooted

Inner field of USize migrating from raw usize to Bits<{cfg-platform-width}, Hot>
for unified bit-storage view. Round 202604500000 explored the direction.
Currently parked. Future round revisits when the platform-width const
generic ergonomics improve.

## Cold strategy bitpacking

Bits<N, Cold> for N > 64 with bitpacked storage across multiple bare
primitives. Out of scope for round 202604271346. Future round.

## Round 3 prerequisites (post-202605021800 work)

Round 3 (#313) of the post-202605021600 substrate-fundamentals work
generalises Mask\<W\> over Bits, with Mask256 collapsing from a hand-
rolled \[QWord\<Hot\>; 4\] struct to a type alias over
Mask\<Bits\<{Width::W256}, Hot, Unsigned\>\>. The work depends on
Round 1's MultiContainer BitPrim impl (round 202605021800) being
landed first; that is now landed.

Round 3 also lifts BitPrim::WIDTH from u16 to USize (was originally
deferred to Round 4 in the prior round split; reassigned to Round 3
during the round 202605021800 expansion since the lift naturally
cascades from MultiContainer's WIDTH = HiT::WIDTH + LoT::WIDTH body
needing USize-additive arithmetic).

## Round 202605021200 follow-ups

- ISize: signed platform-pointer-width companion to USize. Round 202605021200 punted on the call. Arvo's signed needs are met today by IFixed and IBits, not platform-width signed integers. Ship if a consumer surfaces signed-platform-pointer arithmetic as load-bearing.
- USize and Cap checked-arithmetic helpers (checked_add returning Maybe of USize). Round 202605021200 documented overflow as matching primitive usize (panic on debug-asserts, wrap on release). A Maybe-returning shim ships when a consumer surfaces overflow-as-error semantic.
- Workspace lint rule forbidding .0 field-access on arvo primitives outside the implementing crate. The const-trait surface from round 202605021200 is the typed access path; the lint enforces it once the round 202605021400 sweep validates that no false-positive call sites remain. Lives in mockspace-hilavitkutin-stack-lints.

